    {
      "bbox": [
        354,
        288,
        1140,
        386
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, The New York State Financial Emergency Act for the City of New York requires that all liabilities, obligations and disbursements of the City and covered organizations be in accordance with the Financial Plan approved by the Emergency Financial Control Board; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3422,
          "min": -1.9835
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 48,
          "mean": -0.0113,
          "min": -0.2754
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 15576,
        "area_px": 78900,
        "density": 0.19741,
        "chars": 271,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 17.4
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        351,
        362,
        1137,
        440
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, The New York City Charter empowers and charges the Mayor with the responsibility of administering the Expense Budget for the Fiscal Year 1977 (the \"Budget\") ; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.322,
          "min": -1.9955
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 38,
          "mean": -0.0362,
          "min": -0.7654
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 10516,
        "area_px": 62331,
        "density": 0.16871,
        "chars": 171,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 16.26
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        347,
        418,
        1135,
        537
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, The Terms and Conditions of the Budget provide that the Mayor may establish for any agency a quarterly allotment plan which may set forth for the quarter of the fiscal year during which it is to remain in effect (1) rates of expenditure for personal services; (2) ceilings on the total number of personnel; and (3) the total amount of funds to be spent by the agency during such quarter; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3175,
          "min": -1.8862
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 84,
          "mean": -0.0065,
          "min": -0.4813
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 21002,
        "area_px": 95711,
        "density": 0.21943,
        "chars": 400,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 19.05
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        345,
        511,
        1130,
        593
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, The Mayor has determined that the establishment of quarterly allocations and personnel ceilings for each agency is necessary in order to ensure compliance with the Financial Plan and the Budget.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3267,
          "min": -2.1352
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0002
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 34,
          "mean": -0.0125,
          "min": -0.3725
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 13866,
        "area_px": 66192,
        "density": 0.20948,
        "chars": 203,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 14.64
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        341,
        568,
        1129,
        661
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Now, therefore, pursuant to the power vested in me by the provisions of Section 123 of the New York City Charter and a resolution of the Emergency Financial Control Board dated June 4, 1976, concerning reporting and control of covered organization revenues and expenses, it is hereby ordered as follows:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3091,
          "min": -1.8611
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0002
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 64,
          "mean": -0.0023,
          "min": -0.1247
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 16502,
        "area_px": 74354,
        "density": 0.22194,
        "chars": 303,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 18.36
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        336,
        644,
        1127,
        809
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 1. Limitation on Agency Expenditures. The Budget appropriations of all agencies shall be expended in accordance with the quarterly allocations and personnel ceilings established pursuant to Section 2 of this Executive Order. The term \"agency\" as used in this Executive Order means any office, administration, department, division, board, bureau, commission, corporation, institution or other unit of government, including without limitation \"covered organizations\" as defined in the New York State Financial Emergency Act for the City of New York, the expenses of which are paid in whole or in part from the City Treasury.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3074,
          "min": -1.7981
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.3881,
          "min": -0.3881
        },
